Project Initiation Document Date: 23 March 2026

Overall Project Scope

The following areas are within the scope of the project:

BATSA and protection belt countries - Project Jessie
Nigeria - Project Dawn

MEC & NA (GCC & Iran) - Project Paige
Mastermind - Project Harmony

Dubai & UAE manufacturing and ME transit hubs - Project Ebony

Out of scope of this project:

Algeria is out of scope but may be included within the scope of the project at a later date.

Overall Method of Approach

The ownership of AIT strategy has been changed during the Phoenix project and now lies with Finance

Directors. The project assumes that this ownership will be maintained for the period of this project.

As a principle, security and AIT will be combined headcount in most markets but the recommendation for

priority markets is to establish a separate headcount for AIT.

Ensure an AIT approach coordinated across AME Region, addressing value, suppliers and manufacturers.
Robust tracking procedure (feedback reports, reviews, audit visits).

Build capacity.

The project is divided into five workstreams. The workstreams will be managed through a combination of full

time and part time Work Stream Managers. All resources are currently BAT personnel.

Project Deliverables

Many of the workstream deliverables will be business as usual. Only major milestones that will

contribute to the success of the project are listed below.

