Tangible Benefits

e Increase volumes due to a reduction in illicit trade.

e Success against illegal competitors.

Intangible Benefits

e Brand integrity protection

Protection of BAT profit pool

Creating an opportunity for further profit growth

Protection of Consumers from inferior products e.g. counterfeits

Demonstrate Responsibility by working with all legitimate stakeholders against illicit trade

Level Playing Field

Minimise revenue loss to governments

Barriers to competition entry

Protects SOM from smuggling, dumping etc.

Benefits Realisation

On average the gross margin in AME, is GBP 8.6 per mille for the 2007 budget. Every 100 million sticks create
on average GBP 860k in gross margin for AME.

Cost and Timescale

Costs: Workstream costs will be carried by each separate workstream. Where appropriate, workstream

managers and SRO’s should raise cost concerns.

Timescale: Due to the nature of the fight against illicit trade the workstreams will not really end and will revert
back to business as usual. The project will address specific deliverables, but illicit trade will not go away and
opportunities to smuggle will continue to flourish for illegal operators due to high price differentials across
borders, high value, porous borders and low enforcement. The project will deliver benefits and level the playing
field for the project period but the long term benefit of delivering an AIT culture should ensure appropriate

attention and the ongoing fight against illicit trade.

